WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:05.700
So now that we've got an understanding of the high level networking setup of Unreal,

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.500
we now need to look at the main gameplay systems that interact within the networked

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.509
structure of our game.

4
00:00:11.509 --> 00:00:15.429
So we already know that the game mode is on the server only, but where is everything

5
00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:16.429
else?

6
00:00:16.429 --> 00:00:19.710
We've got a number of gameplay critical classes and as you'd expect they only exist

7
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.190
in certain places.

8
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.059
So first we've got the game mode as we know it only exists on the server.

9
00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:30.910
Next is the game state and this exists on both server and client.

10
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.990
The game instance exists on both server and client but it's not replicated, so each connection

11
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:40.159
will have their own unique instance as well as the server.

12
00:00:40.159 --> 00:00:44.280
The player controller exists on the server and the owning client but never the remote

13
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.240
clients.

14
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.390
Pawns and characters exist on the server and the client and are replicated down.

15
00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.170
Next we've got the player state and this is the same as the game state, it exists

16
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.859
on the server and is replicated down appropriately.

17
00:00:57.859 --> 00:01:02.340
Finally we've got the HUD and any associated user widgets, these are all client only.
